# Findings adjudicated as false positives, one fingerprint per line
# (fingerprint = commit:path:rule-id:line — it carries no secret material).
#
# internal/config/sanitize_test.go — now internal/system/config/sanitize_test.go
# TestRepoBaseline_RulesMatchKnownSecrets asserts that every rule in the
# shipped sanitization baseline still matches a representative example of the
# secret it claims to catch, so a typo in a regex fails the build instead of
# silently disabling redaction. A test for a secret detector has to contain
# secret-shaped strings; these are fabricated for that purpose and were
# confirmed (2026-08-13) never to have been usable credentials.
#
# Scoped to these two findings on purpose. A path-wide allowlist would also
# hide a real secret later added to the same file, which is the file where
# that mistake would be hardest to notice.
